# E17.2b — bitnet.cpp aarch64 build: gcc vs clang (follow-up to E17.2)

Workflow `e17-2-bitnetcpp-crossisa` (workflow_dispatch), pinned bitnet.cpp HEAD at job time.
Rule A: no timing numbers recorded/quoted below.

## Runs
- main, clang, GGML_LLAMAFILE=ON (the E17.2 fix from PR #8/dd59a57): run 33219288705,
  job 99009739570 (aarch64) — FAILED at Build step.
- cm/e17-2b-bitnetcpp-gcc, gcc/g++, GGML_LLAMAFILE=ON, aarch64-only matrix: run 33219483905,
  job 99010330381 — FAILED at Build step, same source line.

## Exact compiler error text

clang (run 33219288705, job 99009739570):
```
/tmp/bitnet-cpp/3rdparty/llama.cpp/ggml/src/ggml-cpu/ggml-cpu.c:1495:40: error: use of undeclared identifier 'src1_cont'
 1495 |         const size_t src1_col_stride = src1_cont || src1->type != vec_dot_type ? i2s_row_size : nb11;
      |                                        ^
1 error generated.
```

gcc (run 33219483905, job 99010330381):
```
/tmp/bitnet-cpp/3rdparty/llama.cpp/ggml/src/ggml-cpu/ggml-cpu.c: In function 'ggml_compute_forward_mul_mat':
/tmp/bitnet-cpp/3rdparty/llama.cpp/ggml/src/ggml-cpu/ggml-cpu.c:1495:40: error: 'src1_cont' undeclared (first use in this function)
 1495 |         const size_t src1_col_stride = src1_cont || src1->type != vec_dot_type ? i2s_row_size : nb11;
      |                                        ^~~~~~~~~
/tmp/bitnet-cpp/3rdparty/llama.cpp/ggml/src/ggml-cpu/ggml-cpu.c:1495:40: note: each undeclared identifier is reported only once for each function it appears in
```

## Finding

The identical error reproduces byte-for-byte (same file, same line, same identifier) under
both clang and gcc, in `ggml_compute_forward_mul_mat`'s I2_S GEMM fast path in the vendored
llama.cpp (`3rdparty/llama.cpp/ggml/src/ggml-cpu/ggml-cpu.c:1495`). This rules out the E17.2
hypothesis that it was a clang-specific diagnostic-strictness issue: `src1_cont` is genuinely
undeclared on this code path for the aarch64 build (`-DBITNET_ARM_TL1=OFF -DGGML_LLAMAFILE=ON`),
regardless of compiler. It is an upstream (vendored llama.cpp) source bug on this build
configuration, not a toolchain quirk — `GGML_LLAMAFILE=ON` (the E17.2 fix for a *different*
manifestation of the same missing-declaration pattern) did not reach this reference.

Net: bitnet.cpp still does not build on aarch64 in the pinned config as of 2026-08-28, with
either compiler. An older bitnet.cpp/llama.cpp commit predating this vendored regression was
not tried (out of scope for this LOW-priority follow-up's budget); pinning to one would be the
next step if a green aarch64 build is ever needed, but is not required for the paper's §2 claim
(the claim is about the *absence* of a cross-ISA identity story for bitnet.cpp, which this
strengthens rather than weakens).

